-- title:
--   Supersingular fibre count times #Aut(E,Cyc) equals #SL₂(ℤ/ℓ')
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$ and a nonzero $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$; let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ for which $q$ is a non-unit of $A$, and write $\kappa$ for its residue field. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa\,M'$ over $\kappa$ whose members are exactly the elements of `ssPlaces q M' κ`, i.e. the places $w$ that are rational (the structure map onto the residue field of $w$ is surjective), satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and have $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of `jGeomGen` in `ssJSet q`. Assume `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the field generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise images of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`) is contained in `fieldBar q M'`, the corresponding base change of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$. Let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` along $A$ with values in `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` — a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue map with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and its residue map, together with a degree- and divisor-compatible map on places — and assume $R_0$ reduces coefficientwise: every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-coefficients lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue is, as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Fix $s\in W$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0\cap A$ such that $A\cap k_0$ (the pullback of $A$ to $k_0$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field, and such that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$. Let $\ell'$ be a prime with $3\le \ell'$, $\ell'\ne q$, $\ell'\nmid M'$, and let $\xi\in k_0$ be a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity. Let $K_\ell$ be the intermediate field of $k_0\subseteq k_0((q))$ equal to the base change to $k_0$ of the function field of $X_H$ of level $(q\ell')^2M'$, with $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell')^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell')^\times$, with $A\cap k_0$ acting compatibly, and let $j_\ell\in K_\ell$ be the nonzero element whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion $j$. Let $E$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ and $\mathrm{Cyc}$ a cyclic subgroup of its affine points with $\#\mathrm{Cyc}=M'$, and assume the valuation subring of $s$ is the pullback, along the inclusion of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` into the full-level field, of the valuation subring of `moduliPlace κ M' E Cyc` (the place attached to the moduli point of $(E,\mathrm{Cyc})$ when $E$ is elliptic and $\mathrm{Cyc}$ is generated by a point of order $M'$, and the $q$-expansion place at infinity otherwise). Then the product of two cardinalities equals $\#\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb Z/\ell')$: first, the number of ideals $y$ of the chart algebra $C=\,$`chartAlgFin` $(A\cap k_0)\,K_\ell\,j_\ell$ (the elements of $K_\ell$ integral over the $(A\cap k_0)$-subalgebra generated by $j_\ell$) which are maximal, contain the image of $\pi_0$, and satisfy: for every $g\in\mathbb Q((q))$ lying in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, such that $g$ has nonnegative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $j$ has nonnegative order, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, whenever the substitution $q\mapsto q^{\ell'}$ applied to the coefficientwise image of $g$ lies in $K_\ell$ and in $C$, then for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals the value at $s$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of that element of $C$ and the image of $c$ lies in $y$; second, the number of endomorphisms $\iota$ of the affine point group of $E$ that belong to `rationalHomSet κ E E` (that is, $\iota=0$ or $\iota$ is given on a cofinite set by fixed bivariate rational functions), are invertible with inverse again in that set, and satisfy $\mathrm{Cyc}.\mathrm{map}\,\iota=\mathrm{Cyc}$.
--
--   This is the orbit-counting step at a supersingular point: the closed points of the special fibre of the $j$-finite chart of the auxiliary level $q\ell'$ model lying over the place $s$ form, after dividing by the automorphisms of the pair $(E,\mathrm{Cyc})$, a set of the size of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z/\ell')$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.natCard_levelAut_stabilizer_eq_natCard_rationalAut_of_moduliPlace`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.natCard_levelAut_stabilizer_eq_natCard_rationalAut_of_moduliPlace), where the same count is reinterpreted as a stabiliser index for the level automorphism action.
